        response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
    }
}
```
Maps `Owner` → `OwnerDto` and responds 201 Created with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.

Note: the pipeline also depends on same-package helper classes `OwnerAddress.java`, `OwnerTelephone.java`, `OwnerEmail.java` (normalization utilities), and escalation types under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/` (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidTelephoneException`, `InvalidEmailException`, `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException`, plus handlers). These map escalations to HTTP status codes.

## 3. Owner entity + firstName/lastName

Entity: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` — `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`, extends `Person`. Its own fields: `address`, `city`, `telephone` (`@Pattern ^\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, E.164), `email`, `registrationDate`, `customerCode`, `householdId`, and `Set<Pet> pets`, with standard getters/setters.

firstName/lastName live in the superclass `Person`:
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`
```java
@MappedSuperclass
public class Person extends BaseEntity {
    @Column(name = "first_name")
